	<item>
		<title>Analysis: Teen Marijuana Use Has Declined Significantly in Adult-Use Legalization States</title>
		<link>https://norml.org/news/2026/10/01/analysis-teen-marijuana-use-has-declined-significantly-in-adult-use-legalization-states/</link>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[NORML]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Thu, 01 Oct 2026 16:35:49 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[2026]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[high school]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[teens]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://norml.org/?post_type=news&#038;p=80801</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[Self-reported marijuana use by high-school students fell in states that legalized adult use, according to an analysis of federal survey data published in <em>Addictive Behaviors</em>. &#8220;These results are consistent with dozens of prior studies,&#8221; NORML&#8217;s Deputy Director said.]]></description>
		</item>
	<item>
		<title>Survey: Patients With Eating Disorders Frequently Report Benefits From Cannabis</title>
		<link>https://norml.org/news/2026/09/17/survey-patients-with-eating-disorders-frequently-report-benefits-from-cannabis/</link>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[NORML]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 14:02:11 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[eating disorders]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[patients]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://norml.org/?post_type=news&#038;p=80655</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[Most respondents with anorexia or bulimia who used cannabis said it eased anxiety around meals, according to survey data published in the <em>Journal of Eating Disorders</em>.]]></description>
